{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויפגשהו ה'", :translit "va'yifgesheihu HaShem", :gloss "and He met him, YHWH"} {:he "ויפגשהו בהר האלהים", :translit "va'yifgesheihu behar ha-Elohim", :gloss "and He met him at the mountain of Elohim"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויפגשהו ה'" "ויפגשהו בהר האלהים"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud relates that the angel of wrath sought to kill Moses because he had delayed circumcising his son. Aaron's meeting with Moses at the mountain of Elohim is understood as providential rescue: Aaron came and assisted him, and by Aaron's merit Moses was saved. The narrative links this to Exodus 4:24 where the Lord confronted Moses over the matter of circumcision.", :sources ["Nedarim 31b–32a" "Exodus 4:24" "Exodus 4:27"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויפגשהו ה'" "ויפגשהו בהר האלהים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויפגשהו ה'", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויפגשהו בהר האלהים", :refs ["Exodus 4:27"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:42.687180746Z", :model "glm-5.2"}